{number: 153}
{title: Because He Lives}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] God sent His Son, they called Him [F] Jesus;
He came to [C] heal, love and for-[G7] give;
He lived and [C] died to buy my [F] pardon,
An empty [C] grave is there to [G7] prove my Savior [C] lives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Because He [C] lives, I can face to-[F] morrow,
Because He [C] lives, all fear is [G7] gone;
Because I [C] know He holds the [F] future,
And life is [C] worth the living [G7] just because He [C] lives.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
How [C] sweet to hold a newborn [F] baby
And feel the [C] pride and joy he [G7] gives;
But greater [C] still the calm as-[F] surance:
This child can [C] face uncertain [G7] days because Christ [C] lives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C] then one day I'll cross the [F] river,
I'll fight life's [C] final war with [G7] pain;
And then, as [C] death gives way to [F] victory,
I'll see the [C] lights of glory [G7] and I'll know He [C] lives.
{end_of_verse}
